**Given:**

A boy goes to his school from his house at a speed of 5 km/h and returns at a speed of 10 km/h.

**Formula used:**

Average Speed = dfrac{2ab}{a+b}

Where, a = speed while going, b = speed while returning

**Calculation:**

Average Speed = dfrac{2 times 5 times 10}{5 + 10}

⇒ Average Speed = dfrac{100}{15}

⇒ Average Speed = 6(2/3) km/h

**∴ The correct answer is option (4).**
